#: ../../tools/prosite_tools.rst:32 25266a3b364943078f052174ad83d0f9
msgid ""
"**Description**: Retrieve a PROSITE protein motif/domain entry by its "
"accession number. Returns the entry name, description, type (PATTERN or "
"MATRIX/profile), consensus pattern, functional site annotations, cross-"
"references to UniProt proteins, and documentation links. PROSITE "
"(ExPASy/SIB) contains 1,800+ patterns and profiles describing protein "
"domains, families, and functional sites. Pattern accessions start with "
"PS000xx (e.g., PS00001 for N-glycosylation, PS00028 for zinc finger "
"C2H2). Use this to understand what a PROSITE motif means after finding it"
" via ScanProsite\\_scan\\_protein."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/prosite_tools.rst:34 ../../tools/prosite_tools.rst:65
#: ../../tools/prosite_tools.rst:99 47b3c77bcf034a0aadad594258c62c2a
#: b41f90661b7b419d8764457d629cdea3 d3a19e7e0503437fb69d930a9d8974df
msgid "**Parameters:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/prosite_tools.rst:36 e241e9e2969e4bd898b1f05d2b7bc052
msgid ""
"``accession`` (string) (required) PROSITE accession number starting with "
"'PS'. Examples: 'PS00001' (N-glycosylation site), 'PS00028' (zinc finger "
"C2H2 signature), 'PS00348' (p53 tumor suppressor family), 'PS51420' (Rho "
"GTPase domain profile), 'PS00262' (insulin family signature)."
msgstr ""

